<title>FRANCE: NRJ appeals against CLT's stake in RTL2.</title>
<headline>NRJ appeals against CLT's stake in RTL2.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>French radio group NRJ said on Monday it had filed two appeals against a move by Compagnie Luxembourgeoise de Telediffusion (CLT) to allegedly boost its control over the capital of the RTL2 radio station.</p>
<p>In a statement NRJ said &quot;a financial notice recently published in the press indicated that CLT currently owned 100 percent RTL2 while the only authorised stake made public by (French broadcasting authority) CSA, dated March 7 1995, only permitted it to hold 46 percent..&quot;</p>
<p>NRJ said it had lodged the two appeals with arbitration body, Conseil d'Etat.</p>
